Another issue opened by a user:
"Everything works fine but after integrating a new appimage there's an empty tmp folder left behind in my HOME folder.

Running xubuntu 24.04."

Let me look at the extract script since that's what handles integration.

1 file read
appimage-integrator-extract
Found it. The workdir is $HOME/tmp/$appimage_name/ and it's cleaned up at the end with rm -rf "$workdir", but if the script exits early due to set -euo pipefail (e.g. extraction fails, no desktop file found, etc.), the cleanup never runs.

The fix is a trap to clean up on exit:

Add a trap to ensure workdir is always cleaned up on exit, even on early failure

appimage-integrator-extract
Applied
The trap 'rm -rf "$workdir"' EXIT fires on any exit — normal, error, or signal — so the $HOME/tmp/<appname>/ directory is always removed. The explicit rm -rf "$workdir" at the bottom can stay; it's harmless and makes the intent clear in the happy path.

Worth noting: the same wait_for_file_copy infinite-loop bug from the previous issue also exists in this script. You may want to apply the same fix here too.
